<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/HannahSofa.jpg" alt="A painting of a yellow lab on a sofa" width="550" height="434" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.42857143;">Hannah on the Sofa. 24x30, oil on linen. 2007?</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857143; text-align: left;">This painting of Hannah hangs in our living room. &nbsp;I don't recall exactly when I painted it, but I'm guessing it was 2007 or early 2008.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">At this point I'd been painting in oils for a few years and created this large painting to help with marketing my portraits. It has a sort of photo-realistic look to it which was less than ideal for marketing because it meant I was constantly having to tell people that it wasn't a photograph.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Although Hannah wouldn't stay on the sofa for long periods of time (she doesn't like being stared at), some of this was painted from life. I think I painted her picture left eye 8 or 9 times before I got it close and I'm still not 100% happy with it, but the shadow side of her face and paws is some of the best painting I've done.</p>